Files derived from codex-plugin-cc:
    src/lib/codex/        (app-server.ts, process.ts, protocol.ts, turn.ts, auth.ts)
    tests/fake-codex.mjs

Modifications made by harry, to src/lib/codex/:
    - Ported from JavaScript (.mjs) to TypeScript.
    - Removed the broker transport entirely; Codex runs via the direct
      spawned `codex app-server` transport only.
    - Added token_count / rate-limits handling (rate_limits primary/secondary
      used-percent, plan type, reset time, last token usage) that the source
      did not surface.
    - Added a connect/initialize timeout that tears down the spawned child,
      so a turn cannot hang the host process.
    - Added an already-aborted-signal short-circuit ahead of connect(), so a
      turn cancelled before it starts spawns no codex child at all; upstream
      observes the signal only after connect() has returned.
    - Trimmed to the subset needed by harry's ask/review/fix commands.

Modifications made by harry, to tests/fake-codex.mjs:
    - Deliberately NOT ported to TypeScript, unlike the provider above; it is a
      spawned fixture, not library code.
    - Removed the broker behaviors, matching the provider above.
    - Trimmed to the app-server turn/auth surface.
    - Added harry-specific test behaviors (additive `BEHAVIOR` branches) that
      drive harry's own commands through failure modes the source did not model,
      plus one export (`TRUNCATED_CAUSE`) so a behavior's own message belongs to
      the fixture rather than being hand-copied into each asserting test.

